 # Reconstruction-based Generation
 
-Also called: LGM
 
 ## Overview
-Reconstruction-based Generation decomposes 3D asset creation into two distinct stages: multi-view image synthesis followed by 3D Gaussian reconstruction [S1]. Unlike end-to-end generative models, this approach leverages pre-trained diffusion models to generate posed multi-view images, which then serve as supervision signals for a dedicated Gaussian Splatting (GS) reconstructor [S1]. This method distinguishes itself by reusing mature, standard multi-view reconstruction pipelines, thereby simplifying system-level engineering and reducing the computational overhead associated with direct 3D generation, though it remains subject to the consistency limitations of the initial image generator [S1].
